  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is not in the chain, so it is designated as formyl group.&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0145_02b671f9d3d2.png\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 57px; height: 33px;\" /> group is treated as prefix 'OXO'. The <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> group is described in the suffix as carboxylic acid. Thus, the name is derived from the name of corresponding carboxylic acid.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0145_1a51969fc739.jpg\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 132px;\" />"
  }
